---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import FAQList from '../components/FAQList.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
import { groupTravelPages } from '../data/landing';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Private Group Travel',href:'/private-group-travel/'}];
const faqs=[
 {q:'What is private group travel?',a:'Private group travel is a trip reserved or designed for a specific group rather than individual travelers joining a general public departure. The itinerary, pace, rooming, activities, support, and commercial structure can be shaped around that group.'},
 {q:'How many travelers do we need?',a:'There is no single minimum that applies to every trip. The practical range depends on destination, accommodation, transport, activities, and how fixed costs are shared. We can begin with an estimated range rather than a final number.'},
 {q:'Can we create a trip around our own dates?',a:'Yes, subject to supplier availability, season, local operating conditions, and any permit or event constraints.'},
 {q:'Can Talon help the organizer present the trip to members?',a:'Yes. Organizer support can include helping structure the information participants need to understand the itinerary, inclusions, activity level, likely cost, deadlines, and preparation requirements.'},
 {q:'Can travelers arrive from different cities?',a:'Often. The trip can use coordinated flight planning, a common arrival window, or a destination meeting point depending on the group and itinerary.'}
];
const schema={'@type':'Service',name:'Private Group Travel',description:'Custom private group travel planning for clubs, communities, businesses, studios, teams, friends, and affinity groups.',provider:{'@id':`${Astro.site}#organization`},areaServed:{'@type':'Place',name:'Worldwide'}};
---
<BaseLayout title="Private Group Travel Planning | Talon Expeditions" description="Custom private group travel planning for clubs, communities, businesses, studios, teams, friends, and affinity groups, with itinerary design, organizer support, and worldwide coordination." image={images.group} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} schema={schema}>
  <section class="av-inner-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.group}')`}><div class="shell"><h1>Private Group Travel</h1><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/></div></section>
  <section class="av-detail-main"><div class="shell"><div class="av-detail-gallery"><div class="av-detail-gallery-main" style={`background-image:url('${images.group}')`}></div><div class="av-detail-gallery-stack"><div style={`background-image:url('${images.trekking}')`}></div><div style={`background-image:url('${images.coast}')`}></div></div></div><div class="av-detail-columns"><aside class="av-detail-sidebar"><div class="av-summary-card"><h3>Private Group Planning</h3><p>Build the trip around your people instead of asking your people to fit a generic departure.</p><div class="av-summary-facts"><span>Own dates, subject to availability</span><span>Custom pace and activity level</span><span>Organizer support</span><span>Worldwide destinations</span><span>Flexible support model</span></div></div><div class="av-day-card"><h3>Define the Trip</h3><p>Group, purpose, dates, experience, activity, comfort, budget, and constraints.</p></div><div class="av-day-card"><h3>Shape the Plan</h3><p>Destination, route, lodging, transport, suppliers, support, and likely commercial structure.</p></div><div class="av-day-card"><h3>Prepare to Travel</h3><p>Confirmed travelers, documents, rooming, equipment, flights, final itinerary, and support contacts.</p></div></aside><article class="av-detail-content"><div class="answer-panel"><h2>How does private group travel with Talon work?</h2><p>We begin with the group rather than a fixed tour. Together we define the travelers, purpose, timing, likely size, activity level, comfort, and approximate budget. Talon then develops the itinerary and coordinates the travel structure, local suppliers, participant information, readiness, and organizer support required to move the trip toward departure.</p></div><h2>Custom travel for a group that already has a reason to be together.</h2><p>A private group may be highly experienced and know exactly what it wants to do. Another may have only a community and a broad idea such as a hiking trip next fall or a warm-weather learn-to-dive week. Both are valid starting points. The important thing is to establish the real constraints before expensive commitments are made.</p><p>Private does not necessarily mean luxury, guided every day, or expensive. It means the trip is organized for one group rather than built around strangers joining a fixed calendar. The support level can be light or comprehensive depending on the destination and how much work the organizer wants to carry.</p><h3>What Talon can coordinate</h3><div class="av-highlight-grid"><span>Trip concept & destination</span><span>Itinerary & pacing</span><span>Accommodation & rooming</span><span>Ground transport & arrival logic</span><span>Activities & local specialists</span><span>Organizer support</span><span>Traveler readiness</span><span>Final departure coordination</span></div><section class="av-detail-section"><h2>Customization still needs disciplined tradeoffs.</h2><p>More destinations usually mean more transfers. Higher activity can narrow the group. More private services can raise cost. More free time may reduce how much can be prearranged. A useful planning process makes those tradeoffs visible instead of hiding them behind the word custom.</p><p>Early decisions about purpose, group size, activity, comfort, budget, and support usually matter more than selecting individual hotels before the trip structure is clear.</p></section><section class="av-detail-section"><h2>Questions organizers ask before committing</h2><FAQList items={faqs} openFirst={true}/></section></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section" style="background:var(--av-soft)"><div class="shell"><div class="av-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Explore by Organizer Type</p><h2>Different Communities Create Different Travel Problems</h2></div><p>The deeper pages explain how planning changes for hiking clubs, dive communities, wellness groups, businesses, and social or affinity groups.</p><a class="button button-small" href="/group-travel/">All Group Types</a></div><div class="av-destination-grid">{groupTravelPages.slice(0,3).map((page)=><a class="av-destination-card" href={`/group-travel/${page.slug}/`} style={`background-image:url('${page.hero}')`}><div class="av-destination-card-top"><span>Organizer path</span><span class="av-card-arrow">↗</span></div><h3>{page.title}</h3><p>{page.description}</p></a>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="av-process"><div class="shell av-process-grid"><div class="av-process-visual" style={`background-image:url('${images.planning}')`}><div class="av-process-callout"><h3>Have the Group but Not the Whole Plan?</h3><p>That is a normal place to begin. Bring the people and the reason to go.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-copy"><p class="eyebrow">How it Works</p><h2>A Clear Sequence From Idea to Departure</h2><p class="av-process-lead">The early stages stay flexible while we test fit. Later stages become more specific as suppliers, travelers, payments, and operating details are confirmed.</p><div class="av-process-topline"><strong>See the full process</strong><a href="/how-it-works/">↗</a></div><div class="av-process-steps"><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">◎</div><div><h3>Define the Group</h3><p>Who is traveling, why, and what must work for them?</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">⌖</div><div><h3>Choose the Direction</h3><p>Destination, trip style, season, activity, and likely support.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">▣</div><div><h3>Build the Trip</h3><p>Route, lodging, transport, activities, suppliers, and commercial structure.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">▤</div><div><h3>Prepare Travelers</h3><p>Participant information, documents, rooming, equipment, arrivals, and support.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
